(a) the total kilometers of rural roads constructed and the number of habitations connected from Bagalkot under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) during financial year 2025-26, phase-wise in Karnataka;
(b) the implementation plan for road upgradation and maintenance in Karnataka, if any;
(c) the targets for construction and upgradation of rural roads under the Scheme, State-wise; and
(d) whether any mechanism has been adopted for prioritizing connectivity in aspirational districts, tribal and remote areas, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of schools selected under the PM SHRI Schools scheme as on date;
(b) State-wise and Union Territory-wise details thereof; and
(c) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised in various districts of Karnataka under the scheme during each of the last three years?

(a) the current status of implementation and key achievements of the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijlee Yojana across the country;
(b) the steps being taken to further accelerate the implementation of the Scheme and maximize its benefits for households across the country;
(c) the progress made under the Scheme across Karnataka State with Bagalkot district and the steps taken to facilitate its effective implementation; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to promote wider adoption of the Scheme and enhance its outreach across the State?

(a) the financial and operational performance of major public sector enterprises such as Steel Authority of India Limited (SAIL), National Mineral Development Corporation (NMDC), and MECON during the current financial year, including production, sales, and profit indicators;
(b) the steps taken by these companies to enhance procurement allowing new manufacturers or suppliers to participate in tenders for getting fair prices in procurement;
(c) steps taken to resolve dependence on few companies for procurement and transparency in allocation; and
(d) the new initiatives introduced in promoting digital and human resource transformation?

(a) the details of strategy for mandatory security audits for critical infrastructure units under CERT-In;
(b) the steps being taken by Ministry to address the increasing number of ransomware attacks and cross-border cyber-crime incidents;
(c) whether a National Cyber Resilience Fund (NCRF)has been established to strengthen the industry;
(d) the measures being taken to increase the number of certified cybersecurity professionals in the country; and
(e) the manner in which cybersecurity centres are being expanded to enhance regional cyber incident response effectiveness?

(a) the total amount of funds allocated for NH constructions in Karnataka for the current year and how many projects are under construction;
(b) whether Government has any proposal of extending present Vijaypur -Hubli NH-218 in four lane;
(c) the number of proposed new NH roads passing through district of Bagalkot, Karnataka; 
(d) whether the Ministry propose to make a State level committee from time to time reviewing NH projects of States; and
(e) whether the Ministry will issue necessary directions for NH authorities for timely review of  ongoing roads project of State?

(a) whether any criteria has been prescribed for the selection of gram panchayats eligible for dedicated office infrastructure, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of computers sanctioned to digitally empower panchayats till date in Karnataka and a detailed list of the beneficiary, districts-wise, where these computers have been sanctioned;
(c) the role of these infrastructure and digital initiatives in enhancing service delivery and administrative efficiency under the Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA); and
(d) whether the Ministry has adopted any specific indicators/monitoring mechanisms to assess the impact of infrastructure and digital investments on the functional efficiency of Gram Panchayats?

(a) the procedure for hiring healthcare staff/manpower supply in AIIMS, the terms and conditions of contracts for the same;
(b) the details of service providers supplying healthcare staff in AIIMS, Delhi since last five years on contract basis; and
(c) whether there is any vendor providing such service, even after the expiry of tender by getting extensions, if so, the details of rules in this regard?

(a) whether Government has plan to extend the PM E-DRIVE public transport to semi urban city centres with population of around 80,000 to 1 Lakh; 
(b) whether Ministry has plans for expanding the electric public transport network under PM E-DRIVE at historical places as identified by UNESCO in Badami, Pattadkal, Aihole and Kudal sangam of Bagalkot district, Karnataka for ease of tourists as per request submitted by stakeholders;  
(c) whether there is a roadmap for installing public charging stations across national highways and metro cities; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) measures taken by Government to conserve historical monuments in Karnataka; 
(b) whether Government has any projects proposals pending to be implemented for conservation and development for the revival of heritage sites with historical significance of Ramayan in Seetimani village of Bagalkot District, Karnataka; 
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether actions have been taken for development of the cultural heritage of Seetimani of Bagalkot District, Karnataka?

(a) whether the Ministry has any proposal to develop a jetty for cruise route in Krishna river from Almatti of Vijayapur District to Herkal in Bagalkote District in Karnataka;
(b) if so, the current situation of the proposal; and
(c) if not, whether the Ministry would take initiative to develop a jetty for such cruise route in Krishna river from Almatti to Herkal?

(a) the circumstances leading to the closure of HMT Limited;
(b) the number of employees affected due to closure of HMT and the measures taken for their rehabilitation;
(c) whether Government has explored alternatives to closure, such as joint ventures or strategic partnerships;
(d) the current status of HMT's assets, including land, machinery and intellectual property;
(e) whether there are any plans to utilize HMT's infrastructure for other industrial purposes or initiatives; and
(f) is there any possibility of reviving production line of watches or machines?

(a) the number of smart city projects allotted to the state of Karnataka;
(b) whether Government has planned to include new cities under smart city project; and
(c) whether Government will consider to include Bagalkot city under the smart city projects, as the city has been shifted after submergence from the back water of the Krishna River due to the Lal Bahadur Shastri Dam built on the river basin of the Krishna River and a new city layouts are under construction?
